---
description: Resolve an amendment against an executed edition, trace scoped effects, and gate controlled migration.
args: { request: AmendmentReviewRequest; executed: ExecutedAgreementBundle }
returns: AmendmentProgramResult
uses: [amendmentEngine/frameBaseline, amendmentEngine/resolveOldSectionReference, amendmentEngine/classifyRetroactiveBilling, amendmentEngine/compareOverlappingAmendments, amendmentEngine/revalidateCutover, amendmentEngine/testExceptionPreservation, amendmentEngine/resolveTargets, amendmentEngine/resolveTemporalScope, amendmentEngine/applyOperationsToBaseline, amendmentEngine/walkAffectedDependencies, amendmentEngine/prepareMigrationRelease]
---
Bind baseline = `frameBaseline(request, executed.agreements)` and require its executed-edition hash to equal request.baselineHash. Bind oldSections = `resolveOldSectionReference(request, executed.executedEditions)`, retroactivity = `classifyRetroactiveBilling(request, executed.billingHistory)`, and precedence = `compareOverlappingAmendments(request, executed.overlapEvidence)` before composing text. Ambiguous clause mapping, retroactive authority or overlapping precedence leaves dependent work unresolved.

Bind targets = `resolveTargets(baseline, request.amendmentIds, executed.executedEditions, oldSections)` only when each amendment is mapped to a clause in the executed edition. Bind scope = `resolveTemporalScope(targets, request.effectiveDate, executed.evidencePages)` as explicit interval, entities and excluded cases; do not infer scope from upload order. Bind amended = `applyOperationsToBaseline(baseline, targets, scope, precedence, executed.evidencePages)` using each operation against its target. Keep untouched exceptions and prerequisites in the result. Bind exceptionCheck = `testExceptionPreservation(baseline, amended, executed.exceptionRegressions)` before accepting any deletion; preserve every lost-exception finding as a release blocker.

Bind impacts = `walkAffectedDependencies(amended, executed.evidencePages, executed.cutoverReceipts)` along dependency edges from changed obligations to open tasks, approvals, notices and scheduled work. Keep completed historical acts tied to their old scope. Revalidate every unexecuted task that crosses cutover; a prior approval is not enough. When billing already occurred, propose only a reviewed linked correction from retroactivity and billing evidence; never rewrite the invoice history. Bind cutoverReview = `revalidateCutover(request, executed.cutoverReceipts)` before release. Bind release = `prepareMigrationRelease(request, baseline, targets, scope, amended, impacts, executed.exceptionRegressions, exceptionCheck, cutoverReview)` only after ambiguity, precedence, preservation and reviewer gates clear. Return prior editions intact, impact findings and no publication effect; commitAllowed remains false.